</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... All these posts. Myself included, we still haven't learned our lesson from the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T16:40:05-07:00","id":995427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eddie Fiori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=994747#post994747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of think picking &quot;human&quot; is a bit of a copout.<br /> <br /> In the CofD version of this thread, I interpreted the question as &quot;if you have to be a supernatural, which would you be?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'mma going with Order of Hermes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:28:59-07:00","id":995449,"title":"","content":"Hey, I got an idea, lets have a setting whose sole conceit is that monsters and wizards of legend are real, and <i>you get to play them, and then instead of doing that, you yell AVE HUMANITY at the top of your lungs like you were in goddamn 40k and pretend like that is a superior choice. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>warmerdutch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=995264#post995264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah... All these posts. Myself included, we still haven't learned our lesson from the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apparently the lesson you learned is 'being a prey animal is best.' You are human in real life. Loosen up and pretend a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-29-2016, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:53:49-07:00","id":995455,"title":"","content":"Humans are not necessarily that bad. They use Mythic Numina, Psychic Numina, Qiao, Scientific Numina, True Faith, etc to even the playing field and, against certain foes, humans with Numina are quite effective (beginning Sorcerers created under Equality for All will wipe the floor with beginning Mages who attempt to attack them with True Magick). Mundane humans, however, are very much lunch unless they are in relatively large numbers (ten against a beginning Kindred is not bad odds, but I would want one hundred against a beginning Garou).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T22:22:01-07:00","id":995515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=994989#post994989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if Pentex allows fomori to retire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant Pentex First Team. Not necessarily Fomor. I typed that on pain meds. Ugh.<br /> <br /> And I remember reading in Subsidiaries, that there are the rare few PFT who do manage to retire. Rare as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:39:33-07:00","id":995863,"title":"","content":"a HIT Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:23:19-07:00","id":995876,"title":"","content":"Serious genetic mental health issues affect all but one of my even remotely immediate family, and that's not a small family either. We tend to exist only in the extremes of technically gifted near-autists and emotionally unstable artists, or both at once. Attempted murders, arrests, homelessness, delusions, halucinations, depression, addiction issues, electric shock treatment and suicide are ridiculously familiar experiences for us compared to the general population. With that said on the flip side we have really *really* good genes ageing wise. I've got a 50 year old aunt who looks early-mid 20s still and my great-nan still had rich black hair when she died age 99. Coming as I do from a bunch of ageless crazies I am nothing if I am not a Malkavian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-30-2016, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:27:52-07:00","id":995965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=994503#post994503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Risen. Get to be a Vampire with no weakness to Sun or Fire. Cool powers. Immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not How Risen work. Kindred get eternity. You might get 6 months before you burn out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T01:06:39-07:00","id":995995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=995965#post995965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not How Risen work. Kindred get eternity. You might get 6 months before you burn out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shh. I'm hoping my Vampire ST doesn't figure all of that Shadow stuff out ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T05:45:49-07:00","id":996037,"title":"","content":"Plus, being a corpse is not really that appealing. Risen have real problems associating with mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:39:38-07:00","id":997457,"title":"","content":"Delusions of Grandeur:<br /> Yang imbalanced Face of the Gods it is, me thinks.<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Several options are awesome, like the possibility to interact with both Spirits and Ghosts.<br /> Rites are also a nice touch and overall survivability is not an issue... especially for a Yang imbalanced Face of the Gods.<br /> <br /> Being a Demon would also be very, very nice.<br /> Faith is rather plentiful, the powers are neat and some are seriously powerful.<br /> I am looking at you Rabisu, because they look at Viccisitude, laugh their asses off and do their own thing.<br /> And you can totally start with a Rabisu who has Lore of the Flesh 3... cue the immediate enhancement of physical and mental stats.<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> And even then being a Rabisu it is entirely possible to get the Lores of the Beast, Wild and Flesh easily up to 5 with dedication.<br /> That's a killer combo if I have ever heard of one... hell, even having ONLY Lore of the Flesh 3 would be bad enough.<br /> For Demons in general it is their greatest advantage is that only their level 4 powers and higher incur any faith cost at all.<br /> Making some pacts is probably damn easy and ensures a steady source of host bodies if things go south.<br /> To bad that we never got powers beyond level 5.<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Yeah, Demon it is. Overall they are the pragmatic and easy mode choice.<br /> <br /> The third option would either be a mummy or a being a mage.<br /> Being a mummy can suck, due to the fact that you lack firepower and Balance is a shitty concept which almost ensures that I am not making it very far power wise.<br /> And being judged over and over again is going to suck for sure.<br /> Also, regenerating Sekhem is slow and a serious bottleneck for every endeavour.<br /> So yeah, not a mummy.<br /> <br /> On being a mage: well, Paradox sucks but it is most of the time rather easy to keep in check... unless you HAVE to roll out the big guns once in a while.<br /> So totally doable, but depending when and how I run into some meanie out for blood this might not end well.<br /> Then again, there are many ways to ensure safety depending upon the spheres in question.<br /> <br /> Any option with Rage is right out.<br /> It's a total bummer for interacting with people in normal ways and jumping into killy mode is not fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:32:15-07:00","id":997487,"title":"","content":"Nuwisha for Werewolf<br /> Hollow One for Mage<br /> Demon for the rest (Halaku)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:58:57-08:00","id":999318,"title":"","content":"Homid rokea or dtf devourer, either way either way I am immortal while still being fundamentally alive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:07:46-08:00","id":999477,"title":"","content":"Lately I feel I would like to be a Demon, maybe a Scourge, or a Devil, or even a gloomy Slayer ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T21:21:41-08:00","id":999564,"title":"","content":"A Dark Ages Fae Changeling definitely. Preferably in modern nights but I'll take whenever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T03:43:05-08:00","id":1002817,"title":"","content":"I don't think there are any real downsides to a mage if one doesn't behave in a way that attracts attention. Subtle coincidental stuff is extremely cool on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:14:29-08:00","id":1002939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=1002817#post1002817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there are any real downsides to a mage if one doesn't behave in a way that attracts attention. Subtle coincidental stuff is extremely cool on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I bet you wouldn't limit yourself to coincidental stuff. And humans love to show off.<br /> <br /> And strange things are drawn to mages like moths to the flame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T13:03:40-08:00","id":1003026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=1002939#post1002939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but I bet you wouldn't limit yourself to coincidental stuff. And humans love to show off.<br /> <br /> And strange things are drawn to mages like moths to the flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would. I've been overexposed to people talking about how direct use of magic is evil, so I'd rather not use any obvious direct effects (that can result in both Paradox and pitchfork-mobs), and instead focus on things like empowerment of already-existing human abilities. I'd rather do what I can to erase the division between the mundane and the magical!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:14:39-08:00","id":1003096,"title":"","content":"You know, even coincidental stuff can and will be botched. And actually the best way to bring magic to the world is the direct vulgar spells straight in the face.<br /> The coincidental stuff is too easy to cover up.<br /> <br /> And regarding the strange things...<br /> It could even be that your subconsciousnes weaves an effect from time to time.<br /> <br /> If you know deep down you could do X, but restrain yourself with your mighty will, there will be a time of temptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T00:34:02-08:00","id":1003274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be?p=1003096#post1003096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, even coincidental stuff can and will be botched. And actually the best way to bring magic to the world is the direct vulgar spells straight in the face.<br /> The coincidental stuff is too easy to cover up.<br /> <br /> And regarding the strange things...<br /> It could even be that your subconsciousnes weaves an effect from time to time.<br /> <br /> If you know deep down you could do X, but restrain yourself with your mighty will, there will be a time of temptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it can be botched, but since a botch is likely to cause a Paradox discharge, this problem solves itself. Feeling slightly beaten up for less than 24 hours occasionally seems like a fair cost for all the goodies that even Mind 1 provides.<br /> <br /> As for the erasure of the line between magical and mundane, I don't mean &quot;Throw a fireball&quot;. I mean &quot;Yeah, a person can be so skilled with a katana as to deflect a crossbow bolt or cut through a HMMWV's armour&quot; and &quot;Yeah, a person can be so skilled at handwriting analysis as to have a 95% lie detection rate against total strangers&quot; and &quot;Yeah, Sherlock guessing the safe's code based on just looking at the owner is totally based on things doable in real life&quot; kind of blur between the mundane and the magical.<br /> <br /> It's not about restraining oneself against temptation. It's about being tempted by a <i>different</i> archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:09:08-08:00","id":1003280,"title":"","content":"I agree we disagree \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:27:44-08:00","id":1004240,"title":"","content":"Oooh, it's hard to pick just one.<br /> <br /> If I were a mage, my likely first choice, OoH or orphan would be at the top of my list. On the Convention side, VE would tickle my fancy.<br /> <br /> For the changing breeds, I'd love to be a Bastet, but breed is a tough choice. I like the Ceilican, but the constant change would irritate me. I love the Qualmi, but I detest riddles with the fury of a thousand suns. Pumonca are 'local', so that's nice, but the stark individuality is off putting. So I'd want to be Bastet, but there isn't a breed I'd really be happy with.<br /> <br /> For the Garou, definitely homid and ragabash (given the day I was born). I'd have to be a Child of Gaia. Black Furies would be my first option, but given they dump all their male pups elsewhere... CoG it is. By heritage, I could technically be Get, but I wouldn't survive that. I like the concepts of the Uktena, but again, heritage becomes an issue. All else fails, Glass Walker would be acceptable.<br /> <br /> Edited to add: Mokole would definitely be an option if they had the western version of the zhou lung's draconic forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":753,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","user":"Ariketh","date":". 11-17-2016, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:19:25-08:00","id":1008692,"title":"","content":"Hmm. It would be down to three. Silent Strider Homid ( Philidox) Mage-Akashic Brotherhood<b> (</b>Mo-tzu Fa) and DemonHunter (Shih)<br /> <br /> I've always prefered Wanderlust Detective/Problem Solvers Characters that have a Worldy view. These hitting a good deal of my prefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2